<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranajit Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1722–1769</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranajit Malla was the last Malla king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>, reigning from 1722 to 1769. He completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-gate-bhaktapur">Golden Gate</a> of the royal palace in 1754 and was a patron of Newar music and drama. Rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a> and Patan weakened the valley kingdoms, and in 1769 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> of Gorkha took Bhaktapur and Ranajit went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranajit-malla.jpg" alt="Ranajit Malla" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nyeta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Malla_king_on_his_throne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
